gpui_macos: don't query a tab group before any window can be tabbed

`Window::new` calls `PlatformWindow::tab_bar_visible`, which sends
`-[NSWindow tabGroup]`. On first use AppKit creates the window's tab group and
`NSWindowStackController`. A window can only join a tab group after tabbing
was enabled for some window (a tabbing identifier) or an explicit tabbing
action ran (Merge All Windows, Move Tab to New Window, Show Tab Bar). Track
that process-wide in a flag that never resets, set it in those paths and in
the native overrides, and answer `false` without touching AppKit until then.
After it is set, `tab_bar_visible` queries the tab group as before, so
explicit tabbing and windows whose identifier is cleared stay correct.

Measured on a cold first window (hosted macos-15, debug, Time Profiler): the
`tabGroup` call took ~590 ms wall, 506 ms of it blocked off-CPU.

